I ran the probe as two scenario tests in `master_service_evict_scenario_test.cpp`. Both use `enable_ha` + `enable_oplog` + `enable_offload` + `offload_on_evict`, with `offload_force_evict=false` and one completed, lease-expired 1 KiB object `cold`, followed by `EvictMemory(1.0)`, which goes through `BatchEvict`.

```cpp
// with a local disk (the case in this issue)
auto config = HaConfig(cluster_id);
config.enable_offload = true;
config.offload_on_evict = true;
config.offload_force_evict = false;
MasterScenario scenario("probe batch evict offload with disk", config, backend);
scenario.Given(MemoryNode("memory"))
    .When(MountLocalDisk("memory"))
    .Given(Objects({"cold"}).Size(kObjectSize).By("memory")
               .CompleteOn("memory").ExpiresAt(ExpiredBase()));
scenario.When(EvictMemory(1.0))
    .When(OffloadHeartbeat("memory").ExpectTasks({"cold"}, kObjectSize))
    .Then(Object("cold").IsReadable());
```

The second test is the same without `MountLocalDisk`. There the offload cannot be queued, so with `offload_force_evict=false` the object should stay.

Results on d855a6a (the base of #4723; #4723 does not touch `BatchEvict`). Each test was run 3 times, with the same result every time:

| case | result |
|---|---|
| with local disk | `OffloadHeartbeat(memory) returned 0 offload tasks; expected 1`, then `Object(cold) is not readable: OBJECT_NOT_FOUND` |
| without local disk | `Object(cold) is not readable: OBJECT_NOT_FOUND` |

The log shows `[EVICT-RESULT] evicted_count=1`. I got the same "without disk" result earlier on 129c961.

So both effects reproduce:
- nothing is queued for disk, which is this issue;
- with `offload_force_evict=false`, the only copy is deleted even when the offload cannot be queued.

For comparison, the tenant-watermark pass in #4723 keeps the object in both cases; two regression tests there cover this.

I haven't checked the grouped-object path. If the early return turns out not to be deliberate, I'm happy to send a PR that applies the same ordering to `BatchEvict` (offload decision first, record only right before an actual eviction), with these two tests as regressions.

